.TH AIOWAIT 2
.SH NAME
aiowait \- wait on asynchronous I/O
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "aiowait(fd, level)"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aiowait
causes the calling process to go to sleep until the outstanding I/O
requests by the process to the device referred to by the file descriptor
.I fd
are less then or equal to
.IR level .
The number of outstanding requests is
returned.
If
.I level
is negative, then only the number of outstanding
requests is returned.
.PP
.I fd
is the file descriptor returned by a previous
.B open
of the asynchronous
version of a DMA device, such as a disk or A/D device.
.PP
Since asynchronous I/O is serviced in the order requested, the user can
know when a given request has been completed.
.PP
.B aiowait
is implemented by a call to
.BR ioctl (2)
with the
.B aiocwait
command.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
ioctl(2), async(7)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
A \-1 is returned if the file descriptor is unknown or not a special character
file opened for asynchronous I/O.
.SH NOTES
Asynchronous I/O is non-portable to standard UNIX.
.sp
